Package: horizon-grid
Version: 0.2.5
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: HORIZON GRID <horizon-grid@localhost>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8), curl, ca-certificates
Recommends: docker-ce | docker.io
Suggests: ufw
Installed-Size: 1
Homepage: http://localhost:3000
Description: Self-hosted multi-provider IOC threat-intelligence platform
 HORIZON GRID takes a single indicator of compromise (an IP, domain, URL,
 file hash, or CVE) and queries every configured threat-intelligence
 provider in parallel, correlates the results, and asks an AI model to
 produce an evidence-backed assessment -- all from a self-hosted stack you
 control.
 .
 This package installs the application (a Docker Compose stack: Postgres,
 Redis, Neo4j, OpenSearch, the FastAPI backend, the Next.js frontend, and
 two Celery workers), a CLI setup wizard (`horizon-grid configure`), a
 systemd unit for the running stack, and a desktop launcher.
 .
 Docker Engine with the Compose v2 plugin must already be installed and
 running -- see `horizon-grid check` after installing this package. On
 Debian 12 and Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, the distribution's own docker.io package
 does NOT include the Compose v2 plugin; install Docker via the official
 method instead (curl -fsSL https://get.docker.com | sh, or Docker's own
 apt repository per https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/).
